{
  "manifestComment": "PHASE 1 (Goal 26). Every recorded sample the game plays, with its licence, its source and the peak MEASURED off the shipped file. Generated by tools/audio/build-audio.mjs from tools/audio/recipe.json; do not hand-edit. tests/audio-sample-licences.test.js fails the build if any entry lacks a licence, a source or a required attribution, so a file cannot reach a player without its provenance reaching the credits. Allowed licences are CC0 and CC-BY only — anything with a NonCommercial or ShareAlike term is refused, because this ships on Steam.",
  "_slices": "Spans come from tools/audio/describe-slice.mjs --events, which reports each candidate's peak, attack, decay, sustain and spectral centroid. The drawer picks are the loud ~0 dB spans of the metal till recording, whose 500 ms swell into a hard stop is the drawer running out to the end of its travel; the quieter, brighter spans either side of them are it being pushed back in. Coin picks with a 12-20 ms attack and a 500 ms decay over wood are the FIRST coin into an empty well; coin-drop-with-coins is a coin landing on coins and is what the deep pile plays.",
